the flip and unflippable tables cover exactly the Keyed class: true
every key utils.ml resolves into Utils.settings is flipped through restore_settings, and only those: true
every Keyed key the running backend hashes moves its own component when flipped: true
and no Keyed flip moves a component its classification does not account for: true
every Keyed key outside the running backend's scope moves nothing when flipped: true
no key outside the Keyed class is read while the cache key is computed: true
the key computation reads its Keyed keys per lookup, so the trace sees reads: true
no unflippable Keyed key is read per lookup by the key computation: true
the backend name moves its own component: true
and only components it reaches: true
cc_grid_private_bytes_cap, stated in a child, moves the codegen component alone on a CPU backend, and nothing on a GPU one: true
every child run of the pool-class flips completed: true
no pool-class flip moves a component other than the pool and what follows from it: true
with the chunk count auto, codegen beyond the pool tag moves exactly when the pool width does: true
with the chunk count stated, a pool-class flip moves codegen only through the pool tag: true
the pool component separates exactly the pool decisions that differ: true
each settings-borne key outside Keyed is flipped by restore_settings: true
and moves no component of the cache key: true
no registered non-Keyed key moves the cache key when flipped off its default: true
two fresh builds of the probe compile to the same kernel under the same key: true
every key a compile reads whose class promises an unchanged kernel has oracle values or an exemption: true
no such key changes the emitted kernel while leaving the cache key unchanged: true

Keyed keys this sweep cannot flip in-process:
  backend -- a parameter, not a lookup: backends are process-wide singletons, and the component is the backend name the caller passes -- varied through that argument
  cc_pool_core_class -- resolved once, by the lazy [Cc_backend.pool_restriction] the first compile forces; the pool tag it decides is what the component hashes -- varied in child processes, held to separating exactly the pool decisions that differ and to moving codegen only through that decision: its tag in the limits record, and the auto chunk count its width sets
  cc_grid_private_bytes_cap -- resolved once, by the lazy [C_syntax.per_chunk_private_bytes_cap] the first compile forces; the codegen tag hashes that resolved value -- varied in child processes

Keys a compile reads that the codegen-diff oracle does not flip:
  ll_ident_style -- identifier spelling: the canonical rendering alpha-renames identifiers away, and code that differs only in their names compiles to the same kernel -- a changed text is what the key is right to ignore
  cc_backend_verify_codesign -- a check on the compiled library, which signs it or refuses it and never touches the source: stated on a host without codesign (every Linux CI box) it refuses every compile, so no kernel comes back to compare
  build_files_prefix -- it moves the very artifacts this oracle reads, and Generated refuses a set prefix

Keyed keys hashed only on some backends:
  cc_backend_optimization_level -- CPU backends
  cc_backend_compiler_command -- CPU backends
  cc_backend_arch_flags -- CPU backends
  cc_backend_simd_flags -- CPU backends
  cc_backend_fp_contract -- CPU backends
  cc_backend_fast_math -- CPU backends
  cc_vector_bytes -- CPU backends
  cc_vector_registers -- CPU backends
  cc_fp16_arithmetic -- CPU backends
  cc_parallel_grid -- CPU backends
  cc_grid_min_updates -- CPU backends
  cc_parallel_chunks -- CPU backends
  output_debug_files_in_build_directory -- CUDA and HIP
  gpu_graph_capture -- CUDA and HIP
  gpu_elide_covered_zeros -- GPU backends
  gpu_default_seed_narrow_storage -- CUDA and HIP
